@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 # Activate extensions when needed and manage their runtime setup
 
+**Amended:** [ADR 0041](0041-extensions-compose-through-capabilities-that-pane-brokers.md) (accepted 2026-10-06) adds a gate to activation. A command waits, listed with the reason and running nothing (not its view, schedule, service or root results), while a capability or dependency its package requires is missing, disabled, paused or waiting itself. It comes back by itself when what it needs returns. ADR 0041 also lets a package opt in to an activation entry point, which Pane calls when the generation starts so the package can make its owned registrations. This is an exception to lazy activation that the author chooses, as a continuing service is. Lazy activation otherwise holds. Preserve the original text below; use ADR 0041 for waiting and activation.
+
 **Subsequent setup choice:** Q36 prefers internet-first acquisition of runtime/default-feature payloads instead of bundling them in the installer. The no-manual-tools promise remains. WASI3 components plus optional prebuilt helpers are the current direction under evaluation; exact packaging remains open. See [current decisions](../current-decisions.md).
 
 **Note (#11):** reloading a package starts each of its available commands at once to report a startup failure with Retry; this is a deliberate, provisional exception to lazy activation, recorded in [current decisions](../current-decisions.md).
diff --git a/docs/adr/0011-extension-call-and-result-api.md b/docs/adr/0011-extension-call-and-result-api.md
index a1068979..f79569d0 100644
--- a/docs/adr/0011-extension-call-and-result-api.md
+++ b/docs/adr/0011-extension-call-and-result-api.md
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 # Support extension calls with returned results
 
+**Amended:** [ADR 0041](0041-extensions-compose-through-capabilities-that-pane-brokers.md) (accepted 2026-10-06) adds a second way of addressing calls. A package can provide a named, versioned capability (`<namespace>:<name>@<major>`), and a consumer calls the capability rather than a package. The host brokers each call to the provider the user chose, or fans it out to every provider when the consumer declares that. Anything an extension registers at run time is an owned resource, undone when it is dropped or its generation ends. Published operations, calls by identity and by dependency id, JSON input and result, the error kinds, bounded chains and calls owned by generations still hold. Preserve the original text below; use ADR 0041 for capabilities and owned registrations.
+
 **Subsequent dependency choices:** Q26 accepts installing compatible missing required extensions while optional integrations remain optional; Q27 settles dependent removal. The paragraph below records the original open questions. Concrete protocol, addressing and cancellation remain open. See [current dependencies](../extension-policy-proposal.md#dependencies-on-other-extensions).
 
 **Subsequent contract (#22):** the first protocol, addressing, recursion and cancellation behavior are in [operations](../operations.md): operations published in `pane.json`, addressed by package source identity, JSON input/result, typed lifecycle errors apart from the operation's own, bounded call chains and caller-owned calls. Dependency declaration and installation remain #42.
